.TH OPENGG 1 "November 2026" "opengg 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
opengg \- unofficial SteelSeries GG alternative for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opengg
[\fB\-\-demo\fR] [\fB\-\-minimized\fR] [\fB\-\-lang\fR \fICODE\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-screenshot\fR \fIDIR\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configures the SteelSeries Apex 3 TKL keyboard (8-zone illumination, effects,
brightness) and the Rival 3 Wireless Gen 2 mouse (CPI presets, polling rate,
button mapping, battery level) over HID, with an interface modelled after
SteelSeries GG. The application keeps running in the system tray so that the
keyboard, which has no on-board memory for custom lighting, keeps its colors.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Simulate the supported devices; no hardware is accessed.
.TP
.B \-\-minimized
Start hidden in the system tray.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " CODE"
Override the interface language (en, tr).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Use an alternative configuration file instead of
.IR ~/.config/opengg/config.json .
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print the HID traffic to stderr.
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot " DIR"
Render every page to PNG files in DIR and exit (development aid).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/opengg/config.json
Application settings and device configs.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-opengg.rules
udev rules granting device access to the logged in user.
.SH NOTES
This is an independent community project and is not affiliated with,
endorsed by or supported by SteelSeries.
